; Tile block 2x2 table (cell -> 2x2 character block)
;
; .
;
; .
;
; Four parallel 256-entry lookup tables (#R$7900/$7A00/$7B00/$7C00). A
; background map cell is a single byte, used as the index into all four tables
; at once; the four bytes read out are the four character codes of a 2x2 tile
; block: #R$7900=top-left, $7A00=top-right, $7B00=bottom-left,
; $7C00=bottom-right. The column decoder #R$C941 reads one cell, writes the top
; pair (#R$7900/$7A00) into buffer row A and the bottom pair ($7B00/$7C00) into
; row B, so each cell renders as a 2-char-wide by 2-char-tall tile block. See
; docs/Level-Format.md.
; .
; Page 0: top-left character code of each block.
