; Byte bit-reversal (mirror) table: $9A00[i] = reverse of i's 8 bits
;
; .
;
; .
;
; 256-byte lookup where entry i is i with its bit order reversed (bit 0<->7,
; 1<->6, ...). Used to horizontally mirror sprite bytes: #R$7D98 builds each
; sprite's mirrored half by bit-reversing every other byte through this table,
; and the masked tile blitters (#R$B1BE etc.) XOR the bit-reversed pixel byte
; to draw mirrored sprites.
